-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura on the cusp component: Uₚ reduces to p frob⁻¹
-- statement:
--   The setting is the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring and its Jacobian dictionary, together with the special fibre data at $p$.
--
--   Base data: a prime $p$; a natural number $M$ with $M \neq 0$, $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$; an intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ with `hK` identifying $K$ with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; a discrete valuation domain $A$ with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAp`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$; and an element $j \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the coefficient embedding of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (`hj`), assumed nonzero. Write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) for the resulting two-chart model over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, glued from the finite and infinite $j$-charts.
--
--   Special fibre data: an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra; two proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$, geometrically integral curves $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ together with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of them over $k$ into the base change of $X$ to $k$; the hypothesis `hcover` that every point of that base change lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred`, that the fibre product of $i_1$ and $i_2$ (the crossing locus) is reduced; and a natural number $n$ with `hn` that the crossing locus has exactly $n$ points and `hn0` that $n > 0$.
--
--   Sections: a section $\varepsilon$ of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, sections $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ of $c_1, c_2$, and `hε₁` asserting that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equals the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$.
--
--   Jacobian dictionary: a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation $D$ for $X$ (a scheme $D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ with a zero section), with `hrep` asserting that $D$ represents the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles on $X$ cut out by fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero, relative to $\varepsilon$; `hsm` and `hsep`, that $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is smooth and separated; `hreps`, the corresponding representability over $k$ for the base change of $D$; `hPk`, an isomorphism between the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` and the base change to $k$ of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep`; designations $D_1, D_2$ for $c_1, c_2$ with representability data `hrep₁`, `hrep₂`; a morphism $\nu_2$ over the bases from the base change of $D$ to $D_2$ together with `hν₂`, which for every $k$-scheme $T$ and every $T$-point $a$ of the base change of $D$ gives an isomorphism between the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂` along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ and the rigidification (in the sense of `Scheme.Modules.rigidify`) of the pullback along the curve-change morphism of $i_2$ of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` along $a$. Properness of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ is assumed.
--
--   Geometric generic fibre: compatible algebra structures making $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` an $A$- and $L$-algebra; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), i.e. a proper smooth integral curve with a ring isomorphism of that field with its function field and a bijection of its closed points with the places; an isomorphism $e_\eta$ of $M_\eta.C$ with the base change of $X$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with the structure maps (`heη`); nonemptiness of the preimage of the finite chart under $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection; `hMηpin`, asserting that every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135), read as a germ at the generic point and transported through $M_\eta.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, has Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the expansion of $a$ in $L((q))$; and `hgal`, asserting that for every $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism $g$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise, and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.C$ over the base, if $x'$ composed into the chart equals $g$ precomposed with $x$ so composed, then the place of $x'$ is the image of the place of $x$ under the semilinear action [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) of $g$.
--
--   Special fibre group data: a datum $G$ of type [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9), consisting of abelian groups $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$, a subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus}$ of $G.J0s$ and a surjective homomorphism $G.\mathrm{proj} : G.J0s \to G.JI \times G.JE$ with kernel $G.\mathrm{torus}$; bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` of $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with the $k$-points of the base change of $D$, of $D_1$ and of $D_2$ respectively; hypotheses `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` that these bijections turn addition into tensor product of the pullbacks of the respective Poincaré bundles; and `hproj`, asserting for every $x \in G.J0s$ that `ptsI` of the first component of $G.\mathrm{proj}\,x$ is the composite of `pts x` with the pullback morphism along $i_1$ supplied by `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom`, and `ptsE` of the second component is the composite of `pts x` with $\nu_2$.
--
--   Generic dictionary and Hecke action: a bijection `gpts` of $J_1(Mp)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}) =$ [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the degree-zero divisor class group of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`, with the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D$, additive in the sense of `hgadd` (it carries addition to the relative group law of `hrep`); a family $\varphi$ of endomorphisms of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ indexed by the Hecke polynomial ring [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16) $= \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell, X_n]$, with `hφmul` that each $\varphi(t)$ is additive for the relative group law on $T$-points for all $T$, and `hφpts` that for the Hecke module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129) and all $t$ and $x$, `gpts (t • x)` is `gpts x` followed by $\varphi(t)$.
--
--   Abel–Jacobi data over $L$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: `hDL`, representability over $L$ for the base change of $D$; a morphism `ajL` over $L$ from the base-changed curve to the base-changed designation; a comparison morphism `kL` between the base changes of $X$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and to $L$ with `hkL₁`, `hkL₂` identifying its composites with the two projections; a morphism `ajbar` from $M_\eta.C$ to $D.P$ and a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point `εbar` of $M_\eta.C$; `hPL`, an isomorphism of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` with the base change to $L$ of that of `hrep`; `hajLε`, that the base-changed section followed by `ajL` is the zero section; `hajL`, the defining Abel–Jacobi property, that for every field $K'$, every $K'$-point $t$ of $\operatorname{Spec} L$ and every point $x$ of the base-changed curve over $t$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` along $x$ followed by `ajL` is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the point $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the section; `hajbar`, defining `ajbar` as $e_\eta$ followed by `kL`, `ajL` and the first projection; `hajbar_over`, its compatibility with the base maps; `hεbar` and `hεbar_aj`, that `εbar` lies over $\varepsilon$ and is carried to the zero section by `ajbar`; and `hpts_aj`, asserting that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ lying over $\varepsilon$ there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ equal to the difference of the places of $x$ and of $s$ whose class satisfies $\mathrm{gpts}([D_v]) = x$ followed by `ajbar`.
--
--   Cusp component data: an integral weight one form $w$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$ (a modular form of weight one together with an integral $q$-expansion whose reduction is nonzero); a curve model `Mdl₁` over $k$ of the Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), an isomorphism $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$ with `he₁` over $k$; nonemptiness of the corresponding chart preimage (`hne₁`); `hgauss₁`, the $q$-expansion reading on the cusp component: for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra and all power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction, if the Laurent expansion of $a$ times the image of $y$ equals the image of $x$, then the Laurent expansion of the germ of $a$ on $C_1$, transported through $\mathrm{Mdl}_1.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, equals the reduction of $x$ divided by the reduction of $y$; an additive isomorphism $\theta_1 : G.JI \cong \mathrm{Pic}^0(k, \mathrm{Ig})$ of the Igusa curve; `hθpin₁`, that for $g \in G.JI$ and a $k$-point $x$ of $c_1$, an isomorphism of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₁` along `ptsI g` with the line bundle of the divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of $\varepsilon_1$ forces the existence of a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ equal to the place of $x$ minus the place of $\varepsilon_1$ (transported along $e_1^{-1}$) with $\theta_1 g = [D_v]$; and a semilinear automorphism `frobIg` of the Igusa function field over $k$ (an element of `SemilinearAut`, i.e. a pair of ring automorphisms compatible with the structure map) with `hfrobIg`, that it raises every Laurent coefficient to the $p$-th power.
--
--   Integral subgroup scheme data: a scheme $\mathcal{A}$ with a morphism $a$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a closed immersion $\iota$ of $\mathcal{A}$ into $D.P$ over $a$ (`h𝒜cl`); `h𝒜pr`, `h𝒜sm`, that $a$ is proper and smooth; `h𝒜conn`, that all geometric fibres of $a$ are connected; `h𝒜grp`, that the image of $\mathcal{A}$ is a subgroup for the relative group law in the sense that $T$-points of $\mathcal{A}$ contain a unit and are closed under the multiplication and inversion of the relative group law of `hrep`; `h𝒜gen`, that a class $x \in J_1(Mp)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ lies in the subgroup [`ModularCurve.normFreePartAt (M * p) p`](def/ModularCurve_X1PrimitiveSpecializationAtP.html#L29) if and only if `gpts x` factors through $\iota$; and `h𝒜hecke`, that the image of $\mathcal{A}$ is stable under every $\varphi(t)$.
--
--   Reduction data: a valuation subring $\mathrm{Pl}$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `hPl` asserting that $p$ lies in its nonunits; a ring homomorphism $\rho : A \to \mathrm{Pl}$ with `hρ` compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; a subring $O \le \mathrm{Pl}$ with a homomorphism $\rho_O : A \to O$ and the analogous compatibility `hρO`; a ring homomorphism $\pi_k : \mathrm{Pl} \to k$ with `hAlgk` that the structure map $A \to k$ factors as $\pi_k \circ \rho$; and `hπk`, that $\pi_k$ is surjective.
--
--   Conclusion. For every degree-zero divisor $D_v$ of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying the following support condition: for every place $Q$ in the support of $D_v$ there exist a point $\xi$ of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho$ and a $k$-point $d$ of $c_1$ such that (i) $\xi$ precomposed with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion of $\mathrm{Pl}$ into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equals the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $M_\eta.C$ corresponding to $Q$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection; (ii) $d$ followed by $i_1$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\pi_k$ followed by $\xi$; (iii) no point of $d$ lands in the image of the crossing locus; and (iv) every point of $d$ followed by $i_1$ and the first projection lies in the image of the finite chart $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ — then for every point $zz$ of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho$ with $\mathrm{gpts}([D_v])$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion of $\mathrm{Pl}$ followed by $zz$, and for all $t_0, t' \in G.J0s$ such that `pts t₀` composed with the projection to the base change is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\pi_k$ followed by $zz$, and `pts t'` composed with the projection to the base change is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\pi_k$ followed by $zz$ followed by $\varphi$ of the Hecke generator [`ModularCurve.heckeGenOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L18) at $p$, one has
--   $$\theta_1\bigl((G.\mathrm{proj}\, t')_1\bigr) = p \cdot \bigl(\mathrm{frobIg}^{-1} \cdot \theta_1((G.\mathrm{proj}\, t_0)_1)\bigr)$$
--   in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the Igusa function field, where $p \cdot$ denotes the integer scalar multiple and $\mathrm{frobIg}^{-1} \cdot$ the induced action of the inverse of the coefficientwise $p$-power semilinear automorphism.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura relation on the cusp (Igusa) component of the special fibre of $J_1(Mp)$ at $p$: the reduction of the Hecke operator at $p$ acts on the cusp copy as $p$ times the inverse of the Frobenius semilinear automorphism, i.e. as the Verschiebung. The hypothesis on $D_v$ restricts to divisors whose places all reduce, via the Gauss-type reading of the finite $j$-chart, to points of the cusp component away from the crossings; the result feeds into the version of the statement formulated for classes in the norm-free part, which is the form used in the level-lowering argument.
